---
import Architecture from '../../layouts/Architecture.astro';
import Diagram from '../../components/arch/Diagram.astro';
import Box from '../../components/arch/Box.astro';
import Edge from '../../components/arch/Edge.astro';
import Label from '../../components/arch/Label.astro';
import Cell from '../../components/arch/Cell.astro';
import Legend from '../../components/arch/Legend.astro';

// Big-symbol grid: 5 reels across, 3 cells down, 56px cells, 6px gap.
const CS = 56;
const GAP = 6;
const GX0 = 60;
const GY0 = 60;
const cx = (reel: number) => GX0 + reel * (CS + GAP);
const cy = (cell: number) => GY0 + cell * (CS + GAP);
const inBlock = (r: number, c: number) => r >= 1 && r <= 2 && c >= 0 && c <= 1;
---
<Architecture
  title="Symbols and pooling"
  subtitle="The ReelSymbol lifecycle, the registry, the factory, the pool."
  eyebrow="Cells"
>
  <p>
    A <code>ReelSymbol</code> is one visible cell on a reel, "the thing that actually draws". It is an
    abstract class in <code>packages/pixi-reels/src/symbols/ReelSymbol.ts</code>, it implements
    <code>Disposable</code>, and every visual it shows is a child of its public <code>view: Container</code>.
    Instances are pooled, so a symbol must never assume it was just created: every hook can fire more
    than once per spin and must be idempotent. The symbol knows nothing about its weight, size or draw
    order; that metadata lives in <code>SymbolData</code> and is set on the builder.
  </p>

  <h2>The lifecycle</h2>

  <Diagram width={900} height={470} caption="One instance, one identity, many trips around the ring. The pool is keyed by symbol id, so a recycled 'cherry' only ever comes back as 'cherry'; destroy() is the only way out.">
    <Box x={30} y={30} w={160} h={64} title="create" kind="code" mono={false} sub={['new Class(options)', 'registry.create(id)']} />
    <Box x={330} y={30} w={240} h={64} title="activate(id)" kind="primary" sub={['view reset: visible, alpha 1, scale 1,', 'rotation 0, filters, tint, zIndex 0; onActivate(id)']} />
    <Box x={700} y={140} w={180} h={140} title="on the reel" kind="accent" mono={false} sub={['resize(w, h)', 'onReelSpinStart(joined?)', 'onReelAnticipationStart()', 'onReelSpinEnd()', 'onReelLanded(ctx)', 'playWin() / playDestroy()']} />
    <Box x={330} y={330} w={240} h={64} title="deactivate()" kind="primary" sub={['stopAnimation(); onDeactivate();', "id = '', landing = null, view hidden + reset"]} />
    <Box x={30} y={180} w={160} h={64} title="pooled" kind="muted" mono={false} sub={["symbolId is ''", 'LIFO stack per id']} />
    <Box x={700} y={410} w={180} h={52} title="destroy()" kind="code" sub={['onDestroy(); view.destroy()', 'pool full, or set teardown']} />

    <Edge from={[190, 50]} to={[330, 50]} label="immediately" labelDy={-16} />
    <Edge from={[110, 180]} via={[[110, 140], [250, 140], [250, 80]]} to={[330, 80]} label="acquire hit: pop + reset()" labelDy={-14} />
    <Edge from={[570, 62]} via={[[640, 62], [640, 210]]} to={[700, 210]} label="installed on the strip" labelDx={-2} />
    <Edge from={[790, 280]} via={[[790, 362]]} to={[570, 362]} label="SymbolFactory.release()" labelDy={-14} />
    <Edge from={[330, 362]} via={[[110, 362]]} to={[110, 244]} label="pool.release(id)" labelDy={-14} />
    <Edge from={[450, 394]} via={[[450, 436]]} to={[700, 436]} label="past maxPerKey" style="dashed" labelDy={-14} />
    <Label x={790} y={300} text={['same-id wrap: fast path,', 'stopAnimation() only, no pool trip']} size={10} anchor="middle" />
  </Diagram>

  <div class="not-prose my-8">
    <Legend items={[
      { kind: 'primary', label: 'Template methods', note: 'base class; they call your hooks' }, { kind: 'accent', label: 'Reel-driven hooks', note: 'all no-ops by default, all idempotent' },
      { kind: 'muted', label: 'Pooled', note: 'idle, invisible, id cleared' }, { kind: 'subtle', label: 'Allocation', note: 'dark boxes construct or dispose' },
    ]} />
  </div>

  <p>
    <code>activate(symbolId)</code> stores the id, sets <code>view.visible = true</code>,
    <code>alpha = 1</code>, <code>scale = (1, 1)</code>, <code>rotation = 0</code>, <code>filters = null</code>,
    <code>tint = 0xffffff</code>, <code>zIndex = 0</code>, then calls <code>onActivate(symbolId)</code>.
    <code>deactivate()</code> calls <code>stopAnimation()</code>, <code>onDeactivate()</code>, clears the id
    to <code>''</code> and <code>landing</code> to <code>null</code>, hides the view and resets the same
    properties; the tint is cleared on both sides "so neither half has to trust the other".
    <code>reset()</code> is the pool hook and simply calls <code>deactivate()</code>, so a recycled
    symbol is deactivated twice: in <code>release</code> and again on the way out of the pool.
    <code>destroy()</code> returns early if already destroyed, runs <code>stopAnimation()</code> and
    <code>onDeactivate()</code> if the view is still alive (a game can destroy a container that holds
    it), then <code>onDestroy()</code> and <code>view.destroy({'{ children: true }'})</code>.
  </p>

  <h2>What a subclass implements</h2>

  <div class="not-prose my-6 rounded-xl border border-border bg-card overflow-hidden">
    <table class="w-full text-sm">
      <thead class="bg-muted/60">
        <tr>{['Member', 'Required', 'Default and contract'].map((h) => <th class="text-left px-4 py-2 font-mono text-[11px] uppercase tracking-wider text-muted-foreground">{h}</th>)}</tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {[
          ['onActivate(symbolId)', 'yes', 'swap the texture, restart idle, leave any ended pose'],
          ['onDeactivate()', 'yes', 'pause animations, clear listeners, leave a clean state'],
          ['playWin(): Promise', 'yes', 'resolves when the one-shot finishes; settle it on recycle or await hangs'],
          ['stopAnimation()', 'yes', 'return to idle immediately'],
          ['resize(width, height)', 'yes', 'store the size and reposition children. Runs on every symbol swap. Forgetting it is "the single most common why do my symbols scatter bug"'],
          ['onDestroy()', 'no', 'no-op; release subclass resources here'],
          ['playLanding()', 'no', 'resolves immediately; never called by the engine, for callers that land cells one at a time (Hold & Win lockAnimation)'],
          ['playDestroy({ delay, signal })', 'no', 'the cascade poof: pivot to the bounds centre (position compensated by (c - pivot) * scale), pop to 1.1 over 0.06 s with back.out(2.5), then scale 0 and alpha 0 over 0.14 s with power3.in starting 0.04 s in; about 200 ms. Abort skips to the end. Pivot, position and scale 1 are restored; alpha stays 0'],
          ['playOut(opts) / playIn(opts)', 'no', 'the mystery-reveal seam. Out: scale 0.72 and alpha 0 over 0.18 s, power2.in. In: owns its start pose (visible, alpha 0, scale 0.72), then scale 1 over 0.2 s with back.out(1.7) and alpha 1 over 0.16 s with power2.out. Scale always returns to 1'],
          ['cellInset', 'no', 'null, meaning the art fills the whole cell; sprite subclasses derive it from the texture trim'],
          ['applyCellQuad(quad | null)', 'no', 'curved reels: an affine contain-fit about the quad centre, paid for through the pivot. Must never move view.position'],
          ['onReelSpinStart(joinedMidSpin?)', 'no', 'fires on every strip symbol, buffers included, when the reel enters spin; again with true for each symbol installed mid-spin'],
          ['onReelSpinEnd()', 'no', 'fires just before the bounce'],
          ['onReelAnticipationStart()', 'no', 'fires when the tease begins; relax spin presentation so the strip is readable'],
          ['onReelLanded(ctx)', 'no', "fires before the reel's landing event; ctx = { reelIndex, reelCount, cell, visibleCells, symbolId }"],
        ].map(([m, r, d]) => (
          <tr class="border-t border-border align-top">
            <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs">{m}</td>
            <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs text-muted-foreground">{r}</td>
            <td class="px-4 py-2 text-foreground/80">{d}</td>
          </tr>
        ))}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <p>
    Three more base-class facts. <code>this.gsap</code> is a protected getter bound by the factory;
    animate through it, never through an imported gsap, because a symlinked workspace can load two
    instances. <code>mainAxis</code> (<code>'x' | 'y'</code>) is bound the same way and only motion-blur
    effects read it. <code>landing</code> is the promise started by the latest <code>onReelLanded()</code>,
    set through <code>trackLanding(run)</code> and cleared by the reel when it leaves rest, so a board
    can <code>await symbol.landing</code>.
  </p>

  <h2>Registry, factory, pool</h2>

  <Diagram width={960} height={300} caption="acquire() flows left to right; release() comes back underneath. The registry creates and activates; the factory binds gsap and the axis; the pool only remembers idle instances.">
    <Box x={20} y={40} w={200} h={64} title="Reel" sub={['resize, place, zIndex', "emits symbol:created"]} />
    <Box x={270} y={40} w={200} h={64} title="SymbolFactory" kind="accent" sub={['acquire(id) / release(sym)', 'bindGsap, bindMainAxis']} />
    <Box x={520} y={40} w={200} h={64} title="ObjectPool" kind="code" sub={['Map<id, T[]>, LIFO', 'maxPerKey = capacity']} />
    <Box x={770} y={40} w={170} h={64} title="SymbolRegistry" sub={['register(id, Class, opts)', 'create = new + activate']} size={12} />

    <Edge from={[220, 72]} to={[270, 72]} label="acquire(id)" labelDy={-18} />
    <Edge from={[470, 72]} to={[520, 72]} label="pool.acquire(id)" labelDy={-18} />
    <Edge from={[720, 72]} to={[770, 72]} label="miss: create(id)" style="dashed" labelDy={-18} />

    <Box x={520} y={150} w={200} h={52} title="hit: pop + reset()" kind="muted" mono={false} size={12} sub="reset() is deactivate()" />
    <Edge from={[620, 104]} to={[620, 150]} />
    <Label x={370} y={130} text={['then activate(id), but only if', "symbol.symbolId !== id (fresh ones", 'were activated by the registry)']} size={10} anchor="middle" />

    <Edge from={[105, 104]} via={[[105, 240], [370, 240]]} to={[370, 104]} label="release(symbol)" labelDy={14} />
    <Label x={612} y={262} text="release = deactivate(), view.parentRenderLayer?.detach(view), view.removeFromParent(), pool.release(id, symbol)" size={10} anchor="middle" />
    <Label x={612} y={280} text="pool.release pushes, or disposes with destroy() when the id's stack already holds maxPerKey" size={10} anchor="middle" />
  </Diagram>

  <p>
    <code>SymbolRegistry.register(symbolId, SymbolClass, options)</code> stores one entry per id
    and throws on a duplicate; one class for ten ids means ten calls. <code>create(id)</code> runs
    <code>new SymbolClass(options)</code> and calls <code>activate(id)</code> immediately, throwing
    with the registered list if the id is unknown. The registry has no concept of size, weight or
    zIndex. Registration happens inside <code>builder.symbols(registry =&gt; ...)</code>.
  </p>

  <p>
    <code>SymbolFactory</code> (internal since PR #140) is constructed as
    <code>(registry, maxPoolPerKey = 20, gsap = DEFAULT_GSAP, mainAxis = 'y')</code>. Its pool
    factory is <code>registry.create(key)</code> followed by <code>bindGsap</code> and
    <code>bindMainAxis</code>, bound at create time because a pooled symbol never crosses reel
    sets. Because the pool is keyed by id, a recycled instance never changes identity in reel use;
    that is why <code>CardSymbol</code> can have a no-op <code>onActivate</code> and why
    <code>SpineReelSymbol</code>'s per-id Spine map only ever holds one entry. Identity swaps
    happen only on the <code>prewarmSpinTextures</code> scratch symbol and inside <code>StaticSpinSymbol</code>.
  </p>

  <p>
    <code>ObjectPool&lt;T&gt;</code> in <code>pool/ObjectPool.ts</code> is a public export.
    <code>acquire(key)</code> throws after <code>destroy()</code> (a ticker or promise is outliving
    teardown), pops LIFO and calls <code>reset</code>, or calls the factory on a miss.
    <code>release(key, item)</code> is a no-op after destroy and for an item already pooled (the
    double-release guard prevents aliasing); past <code>maxPerKey</code> the item is disposed.
    There is no pre-allocation and no cap on live objects, only on the retained idle set.
    <code>setMaxPerKey</code> disposes any excess at once.
  </p>

  <pre><code>{`// pool capacity, set by the builder
poolCapacity = builder.poolCapacity(n) ?? max(20, sum over reels of (visible + bufferStart + bufferEnd))
// a MultiWays reel counts at maxCells; the worst case for one id is the whole strip showing it
// DEFAULTS.maxPoolPerKey = 20; ReelSet.addReels() / removeReels() call setCapacityPerKey`}</code></pre>

  <h2>symbolData and draw order</h2>

  <p>
    <code>SymbolData</code> (<code>config/types.ts</code>) carries <code>weight</code>, <code>zIndex?</code>,
    <code>unmask?</code> and <code>size?: {'{ reels, cells }'}</code>. You set it with
    <code>builder.weights({'{...}'})</code> and <code>builder.symbolData({'{...}'})</code>, and the builder
    fills in <code>weight 10</code> and <code>zIndex 1</code> for every registered id; <code>size</code>
    defaults to <code>{'{ reels: 1, cells: 1 }'}</code>. <code>unmask: true</code> lifts the view into
    <code>viewport.unmaskedContainer</code> at rest only.
  </p>

  <pre><code>{`view.zIndex = symbolData.zIndex * 100 + stackingIndex
// stackingIndex = strip array index (cellStacking 'ascending') or length - 1 - index ('descending')
// Z_INDEX_BUDGET.symbolLayer = 100; pin overlays sit at 10000; destroy and swap bumps use 1000`}</code></pre>

  <p>
    zIndex only sorts within one reel's container; cross-reel layering needs <code>unmask: true</code>.
    <code>builder.symbolZIndex(resolver)</code> replaces the formula; the resolver gets
    <code>{'{ symbolId, symbolData, reelIndex, reelCount, arrayIndex, visibleCell | null, visibleCells, atRest, defaultZIndex }'}</code>
    and must be pure and cheap, because it runs after every wrap, snap, swap and rest transition. One
    drift to know: the ReelSet doc table says the default zIndex is <code>?? 0</code>, but the builder
    writes <code>?? 1</code>, so built symbols start at <code>100 + index</code>. The code is the source
    of truth here.
  </p>

  <h2>Big symbols</h2>

  <Diagram width={760} height={300} caption="A 2 x 2 block anchored at reel 1, cell 0. The server sends the id at the anchor only; the other three cells become OCCUPIED stubs, and the anchor's view is resized to cover the whole block, gaps included.">
    {[0, 1, 2, 3, 4].map((r) => [0, 1, 2].map((c) => {
      if (r === 1 && c === 0) return null;
      return <Cell x={cx(r)} y={cy(c)} size={CS} label={inBlock(r, c) ? 'stub' : `${r},${c}`} sub={inBlock(r, c) ? 'OCCUPIED' : undefined} kind={inBlock(r, c) ? 'empty' : 'plain'} />;
    }))}
    <Cell x={cx(1)} y={cy(0)} size={CS} label="anchor" sub="'bonus'" kind="hot" />
    <rect x={cx(1) - 3} y={cy(0) - 3} width={2 * CS + GAP + 6} height={2 * CS + GAP + 6} rx="9" class="guide-strong" style="stroke-dasharray: 4 3" />
    <Edge from={[cx(1), 36]} to={[cx(2) + CS, 36]} arrow="both" label="size.reels = 2 (cross axis)" labelDy={-14} />
    <Edge from={[cx(4) + CS + 14, cy(0)]} to={[cx(4) + CS + 14, cy(1) + CS]} arrow="both" label="size.cells = 2 (main axis)" labelDx={104} />
    <Label x={400} y={170} size={10.5} text={['anchor view resized to _blockSize(w, h):', `2 * ${CS} + ${GAP} = ${2 * CS + GAP} px on each axis here`, 'stubs are invisible; getVisibleGrid() reports', "'bonus' in all four cells"]} />
    <Label x={60} y={270} size={10.5} text={['Declared on the builder, not the registry: symbolData({ bonus: { size: { reels: 2, cells: 2 }, zIndex: 5 } }).', 'Weight must be 0: random fill never places blocks. coordinateBigSymbols() validates and paints the stubs.']} />
  </Diagram>

  <p>
    <code>size.reels</code> runs along the cross axis and <code>size.cells</code> along the main axis
    whatever the orientation. <code>coordinateBigSymbols</code> (<code>spin/bigSymbolBlocks.ts</code>) is
    pure, runs in the SpinController before any per-reel <code>FrameBuilder.build()</code>, throws with
    a named message when a block does not fit, and is on every path that puts a grid on the reels:
    landing, <code>initialFrame</code>, <code>addReels</code>, <code>addRows</code>, <code>removeRows</code>,
    <code>pin</code> and <code>movePin</code>. An anchor may sit in <code>bufferStart</code> with its tail
    visible, and stubs may spill into <code>bufferEnd</code>. <code>OccupiedStub</code> is an internal
    <code>ReelSymbol</code> in <code>core/Reel.ts</code> that sets alpha 0 and visible false on activate;
    it is not pooled through the factory but allocated lazily per reel and reused. Big symbols cannot
    be combined with <code>multiways()</code>, a non-anchor cell cannot be pinned, and a block spanning
    reels with mismatched cell sizes logs a one-time warning. The recipe convention for anchors is
    <code>zIndex: 5</code>. See <a href="/guides/big-symbols/">the big symbols guide</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>The concrete classes</h2>

  <div class="not-prose my-6 rounded-xl border border-border bg-card overflow-hidden">
    <table class="w-full text-sm">
      <thead class="bg-muted/60">
        <tr>{['Class', 'Options and defaults', 'Behaviour'].map((h) => <th class="text-left px-4 py-2 font-mono text-[11px] uppercase tracking-wider text-muted-foreground">{h}</th>)}</tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {[
          ['SpriteSymbol', 'textures: Record<id, Texture>; anchor, in code { 0, 0 }', 'onActivate swaps the texture and syncs the perspective mesh. playWin: scale pulse to 1.15 over 0.15 s, yoyo, one repeat, power2.inOut; _killWinTween always settles a pending await. resize sets sprite width and height only. On curved reels it draws through a PerspectiveMesh and falls back to the affine fit for atlas sub-frames; cellInset comes from the texture trim.'],
          ['AnimatedSpriteSymbol', 'frames: Record<id, Texture[]>; animationSpeed 1; anchor, in code { 0, 0 }; loop = false', 'onActivate sets textures and gotoAndStop(0). playWin is gotoAndPlay(0), returning to frame 0 on complete. onFrameChange pushes every frame to the perspective mesh so a curved win does not freeze. resize sets the size and positions the sprite at size * anchor.'],
          ['SpineSymbol (core, optional peer)', "skeletonDataMap; idleAnimation 'idle'; winAnimation 'win'; defaultSkin 'default'; strict false", 'Loaded by a dynamic import; constructing before whenSpineReady() resolves throws. One Spine per instance, rebuilt on a new id, idle looped on track 0. playWin plays win once; listener on the TrackEntry. onDeactivate settles the win and clearTracks() only. resize is a non-uniform stretch from getBounds() with no positioning; from reading the code, a second resize at the same size can undo the fit because getBounds() includes the current scale.'],
          ['SpineReelSymbol (pixi-reels/spine)', "spineMap { skeleton, atlas, skin? }; idle 'idle', win 'win', landing 'landing', out 'disintegration', blur 'blur'; animations overrides per id; scale 1; autoPlayBlur false; autoPlayLanding false | fn", 'One Spine per id, parked (visible false, autoUpdate false) when not on screen, update(0) on activate so a snapshot sees the pose. playOneShot(name, { track = 0, then }) returns a promise settled on complete, interrupt or end; then defaults to idle on track 0 and clear elsewhere, hold keeps an overlay. playWin, playLanding (via trackLanding) and playOut (then: hold) are built on it. playDestroy plays the out animation or falls back to the base poof. playBlur is idempotent. onDeactivate settles one-shots, clearTracks, setToSetupPose, parks. resize re-centres only: no fit-scaling, author at cell size or use scale.'],
          ['CardSymbol (debug)', 'color; label; textColor 0xffffff; font Roboto Condensed 32 bold', 'identity fixed at construction, so onActivate and onDeactivate are no-ops. playWin: glyph to 1.4 over 0.18 s with back.out(2), a rotation wobble of 0.12 rad, back to 1 at 0.32 s, fill flashes 0xffe168 at 0.06 s and restores at 0.42 s. resize draws a (0, 0, w, h) rect with an inset 2 px stroke at alpha 0.25 and sets fontSize = max(7, floor(min(0.38 * h, 0.7 * w / (len * 0.45)))). Exports CARD_DECK (7, 8, 9, 10, J, Q, K, A) and WILD_CARD.'],
          ['PhaseCardSymbol (debug)', 'label; textColor; colors; landedMs 350', "extends CardSymbol. setPhase(phase) repaints; 'landed' reverts to 'rest' after landedMs. static watch(reels) subscribes to phase:enter, landed and symbol:created and returns an unsubscribe."],
          ['EmptySymbol', 'none', 'every hook is a no-op; renders nothing. Hold & Win blanks, cascade holes, placeholders. HoldAndWinBuilder registers it under emptyId.'],
          ['OccupiedStub (internal)', 'none', 'invisible filler for non-anchor big-symbol cells; allocated by the Reel, not the factory.'],
          ['StaticSpinSymbol + SpinTextureCache', "createInner; cache; spinTexture 'blurred'; blurRampMs 120; blur (axis = the set's mainAxis)", 'Wraps an inner symbol. On spin start it captures a crisp snapshot while the inner is still live, crossfades to a pre-baked blur over 120 ms, then deactivates the inner so it costs nothing while spinning. Anticipation fades the blur out. On spin end it reactivates the inner on the final id. The cache is one per reel set, keyed by id plus size (rounded to 0.001 px) plus axis; blur strength defaults to 0.2 of the cell, quality 4, padding ceil(strength), baked once with no per-frame filter. prewarmSpinTextures() fills it at load time.'],
        ].map(([c, o, b]) => (
          <tr class="border-t border-border align-top">
            <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs">{c}</td>
            <td class="px-4 py-2 text-foreground/80 text-xs">{o}</td>
            <td class="px-4 py-2 text-foreground/80">{b}</td>
          </tr>
        ))}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h3>The Spine animation vocabulary</h3>

  <div class="not-prose my-6 rounded-xl border border-border bg-card overflow-hidden">
    <table class="w-full text-sm">
      <thead class="bg-muted/60">
        <tr>{['Role', 'Default name', 'Loops', 'How it plays'].map((h) => <th class="text-left px-4 py-2 font-mono text-[11px] uppercase tracking-wider text-muted-foreground">{h}</th>)}</tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {[
          ['Resting', 'idle', 'yes', 'automatically on activate'],
          ['Reel-stop one-shot', 'landing', 'no', 'playLanding() or autoPlayLanding'],
          ['Win', 'win', 'no', 'playWin()'],
          ['Cascade pop / exit', 'disintegration', 'no', 'playOut() / playDestroy()'],
          ['Fast spin', 'blur', 'yes', 'playBlur() or autoPlayBlur'],
          ['Neighbour cue', 'reactions/react_{u,d,l,r,ul,ur,dl,dr}', 'no', 'raw spine.state, or playOneShot(name, { track: 1 })'],
        ].map((row) => (
          <tr class="border-t border-border">
            {row.map((v, i) => <td class:list={['px-4 py-2', i === 1 ? 'font-mono text-xs' : 'text-foreground/80']}>{v}</td>)}
          </tr>
        ))}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <p>
    A missing animation is a silent no-op; the library never throws on one, and the core
    <code>SpineSymbol</code>'s <code>strict</code> mode is the opt-in exception (ADR 011). The listener
    rule: attach completion listeners to <code>TrackEntry.listener</code>, never <code>state.addListener</code>,
    and null the listener on settle because Spine pools track entries. Never clear state listeners
    during the symbol's life, since the game may have added some; <code>clearListeners()</code> runs only
    in <code>onDestroy</code>. Removing a state listener mid-dispatch once made other listeners miss
    events. The Spine runtime stays out of the core bundle: import <code>SpineReelSymbol</code> only from
    <code>pixi-reels/spine</code>.
  </p>

  <p>
    <code>PHASE_CARD_COLORS</code>, the palette <code>PhaseCardSymbol</code> paints with: rest <code>0x4b5563</code>,
    start <code>0x38bdf8</code>, spin <code>0x2563eb</code>, anticipation <code>0xf59e0b</code>, stop <code>0x8b5cf6</code>,
    landed <code>0x22c55e</code>, adjust <code>0xec4899</code>, cascade:fall <code>0x0ea5e9</code>, cascade:place
    <code>0x14b8a6</code>, cascade:dropIn <code>0x06b6d4</code>, other <code>0x9ca3af</code>.
  </p>

  <h2>Random-draw pools and scopes</h2>

  <p>
    These are a different thing from the object pool. A <code>SymbolPool</code> is
    <code>{'{ weights?, exclude? }'}</code>; a weight of 0 removes an id as fully as excluding it.
    A scope is <code>{'{ reel?, slots? }'}</code> with slots one of <code>'spinning'</code> (every
    random draw, the default), <code>'buffer'</code> (both off-window sides), <code>'bufferStart'</code>
    (the smaller-coordinate side: above on vertical, left on horizontal) or <code>'bufferEnd'</code>.
    Layers resolve widest first:
  </p>

  <pre><code>{`base weights -> global spinning -> per-reel spinning -> global buffer -> per-reel buffer -> global side -> per-reel side
// weights override per id; exclusions accumulate: a narrower layer can only ban more, never re-admit
// changes apply to the next draw; symbols already on the strip stay until they wrap out`}</code></pre>

  <p>
    At build time pools come from <code>builder.randomSymbols(pool, scope)</code>; at runtime
    <code>reelSet.randomSymbols</code> exposes <code>set(pool | null, scope?)</code>, <code>clear()</code>
    and <code>weights(scope?)</code>. The provider validates every id, compiles every reachable table,
    and rolls back with <code>No symbol left to draw for ... cells on reel N</code> if a scope would be
    empty. Draws are a binary search over cached cumulative-weight tables with the injected
    <code>rng</code> (<code>builder.rng(fn)</code>, default <code>Math.random</code>).
    See <a href="/architecture/frame-pipeline/">the frame pipeline</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Conventions and gotchas</h2>

  <ul>
    <li><strong>The anchor is 0,0.</strong> The view's local origin is the cell's top-left; the reel places <code>view</code> there and reads <code>view.position</code> back to find the slot, so a symbol must never move its own position. Curve fits and destroy tweens use the pivot instead. The option docs for <code>SpriteSymbol</code> and <code>AnimatedSpriteSymbol</code> say the anchor defaults to 0.5, but the code defaults to 0,0 and <code>SpriteSymbol.resize</code> does not compensate for an anchor; the code is the source of truth here, and anchor 0,0 is the safe convention.</li>
    <li><strong>resize is critical.</strong> It runs on every symbol swap. Store the size and reposition children; do not assume an anchor centres anything.</li>
    <li><strong>Settle every promise on recycle.</strong> Sprite <code>_killWinTween</code>, AnimatedSprite <code>stopAnimation</code>, Spine <code>_settleWin</code> and <code>_settleOneShots</code>, Card <code>_endWin</code>. Otherwise an <code>await playWin()</code> hangs forever.</li>
    <li><strong>The same-id fast path</strong> skips deactivate and activate entirely, so the reel calls <code>stopAnimation()</code> itself and resets alpha, scale, rotation, filters and tint. No <code>symbol:created</code> fires.</li>
    <li><strong>Parked Spines do not tick.</strong> Only the on-screen Spine has <code>autoUpdate</code>, which matters with hundreds of cells on a Hold &amp; Win board. Reset to the setup pose on deactivate, or a disintegrated symbol comes back invisible.</li>
    <li><strong>Pools and tests.</strong> <code>HeadlessSymbol</code> from <code>pixi-reels/testing</code> is a <code>ReelSymbol</code> that draws nothing; the whole lifecycle above runs in Node without a renderer.</li>
  </ul>

